# Citation metadata for PlastidToolSuite (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# Authorship note (deliberate, 11/10/2026): the author below is the project, not a list of people.
# Who is named on a citable artifact is the team's decision, and it must be settled BEFORE the
# DOI is minted — a Zenodo deposit records its authors permanently. Replace `authors` with the
# real list at that point; the rest of this file needs no change.
#
# `doi:` and `date-released:` are absent on purpose: the release's DOI does not exist until Zenodo
# mints it from the GitHub release, and the date does not exist until the tag does
# (docs/release.md). A placeholder here would be the kind of plausible-looking untruth this project
# exists to avoid.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PlastidToolSuite in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "PlastidToolSuite: a toolkit for plastid and mitochondrial genome analysis"
abstract: >-
  A command-line toolkit for plastid (chloroplast) genome analysis: assembly from short or HiFi
  reads with the read support checked, annotation by reference transfer, genome statistics and
  structure, gene content, codon usage, introns, SSR, repeats, substitutions (Ts/Tv), nucleotide
  diversity, barcodes, Ka/Ks, population genetics, synteny, maximum-likelihood phylogeny, predicted
  RNA-editing sites, gene-name unification and NCBI submission files, with a prototype path for
  mitochondrial genomes. Every run writes its own directory with its tables, a draft report, and
  the name, version and command line of every external tool it used.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PlastidToolSuite contributors"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/tridovan/plastid-suite/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tridovan/plastid-suite"
url: "https://github.com/tridovan/plastid-suite"
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - plastome
  - chloroplast genome
  - mitochondrial genome
  - bioinformatics
  - comparative genomics
  - microsatellites
  - codon usage
